So today I started off another new character, a samurai. I found a sack
on DLVL 2 that I figured must just be a normal sack (I'm not that
lucky). Handy though, so I keep it. Then I find a tool shop on the same
DLVL with not one, not two, but THREE sacks that cost 133 gold each.
Yippee! I'm pretty confident that at least one of them is a BoH (as
opposed to oilskin sack which costs the same amount). Note: It was a
huge tool shop,  There was a plate mail earlier in the level, so there
was a perfect opportunity to #name a BoH, should any of these sacks
turn out to be one. I put the plate mail in one of the bags... "Your
movements are now unencumbered." Yay! I #name this sack "bag of
holding" and to my surprise, EVERY sack that I've found so far becomes
"a sack named bag of holding." So here I am, dungeon level 2 and there
are four bags of holding in the game.

After a bit more adventuring in the first level of the mines I kill a
gnome and what did he have?? Another BoH! I figure this is just the
game toying with me, since my last game I was burdened for a very
considerable amount of time due to there being not a single BoH in the
game.

And I'm sure you can guess what comes next... my "prize" for Sokoban
is...yet another BoH. Pretty ridiculous, eh? At least I can look
forward to being unencumbered the rest of the game. I can probably also
look forward to being disintegrated by a death ray. I would much rather
receive an Amulet of Reflection from Sokoban than a BoH, even if I
desperately need both.



